	(text "Detector (U2A/U2B): Fig. 6 values. U2A gives -Vin on positive half-cycles; U2B sums Vin (R4) and 2x that (R3),\ngiving |Vin|, and charges C2 through D3 + R6. Attack R6*C2 ~ 1.7 ms; decay R5total*C2 ~ 0.7 s (about 1.6 s to -20 dB).\nGain = R5total/R4, R5total = R5 + RV1 = 200k-220k (gain 1.00-1.10). Set RV1 so 3.474 Vpp (+4 dBu) just lights the 0 dB lamp\n(about 1.74 V at C2). The trim covers the ~2.6% peak sag, resistor tolerance and LM3916 scale spread.\nC2 must be film (value sets ballistics). C2 is unbuffered: drive only the LM3916 input (through R22).\n\nBar: RHI = REF OUT = 1.25 V x (1 + R8/R7) + I_ADJ x R8 ~ 2.46 V; 0 dB lamp (pin 13) at 0.708 x RHI.\nLED current ~ 10 x (1.25 V / R7 + RHI / divider[8-17k]) ~ 5.5 mA per segment. Green shunts R11-R17\ntuned on the bench; yellow shunts R18-R20 DNP. LED order: pin 1 = -20 dB ... pin 10 = +3 dB.\n\nPeak LED (U2C): trips when AUDIO_IN peak > RHI x (R23 + R24) / R24 ~ 12 Vpp. R25 protects RHI when\n+/-15 V is off (TL074H inputs are diode-clamped to its rails). C3 holds; it discharges through R26 into\nQ1's base, so the LED fades out over ~0.5 s. Positive peaks only.\n\nSupplies: +5 V (LM3916, LEDs) about 70 mA at full scale; +/-15 V (U2) about 5 mA."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
